+Running an available, non-guarded check yourself (a build, typecheck, curl,
+`terraform validate`) as a debugging aid is routine authorized work and does not
+require asking first — but it never substitutes for the sign-off itself.
+Verification is a developer confirmation gate, not something self-certified because
+a command exited 0 in your sandbox: your sandbox is not the developer's machine, and
+tool availability, versions, or network behavior can differ. Report exactly what you
+ran and its real result, then still present every verification item from the plan
+and stop and wait; a self-run check answers whether it passed for you, never whether
+the developer signs off to proceed. Having Bash access, or a delegated worker lacking
+a tool, is never a reason to take a sign-off gate over yourself.
 
